{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7xuSEzWBz4gyRxVBGC5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I withdrew node `NRS_484B_267_2f_o2` and sent it back to the planner, with no gap filed. It can't be repaired as a record, so `record.jsonl` holds a single withdrawal on span `s11r`, kind `plan`.\n\n**Why it can't be repaired:** the node's whole duty is \"proceed as required pursuant to NRS 484B.607\", and that law isn't in this run. No NRS 484B.607 node exists, so `s11r` can't be written as a compliance composition. The record therefore has no obligation, which is why the coder's rule ended with an always-true placeholder (`.tt`). Its `forbid` and `permit` scenarios assume what NRS 484B.607 requires (slowing down, moving to a lane not next to the stopped vehicle), so `forbid` came out compliant. Writing \"keeps moving\" from `kin.speed` would set a weaker duty than the words state, and it would still fail `forbid`.\n\n**What the planner needs to do:** add NRS 484B.607 (lines 1a–1d) to the plan. Then `s11r` can be written as a compliance composition, the same way the sibling node `NRS_484B_267_2f_o1` handles its reference to subsection 1.\n\n**A second problem, noted in the withdrawal for the same re-plan:** the borrowed words \"visible from the front\" need the warning lamp's facing. The formula atom `sig_warning_lamp` reads only colour and mode. This is the same failure that `NRS_484B_267_1a`, `1b_o2` and `1c` got back from the gate. It should be filed as an operator gap on the trigger span, not narrowed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1667,"cache_read_input_tokens":92385,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1667},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"us","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management"